{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbZpPTtous3QuJWuMBNK", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "That's a frustrating way to lose two hours. I saved it as a high-priority warning in the project's EngramDB memory. Future sessions will be told to check `PAYMENTS_LIVE` first if payments look wrong.\n\n**The code that reads `PAYMENTS_LIVE` isn't in this repo.** Nothing here mentions the variable. `src/api/checkout.py` just adds up the cart and returns `\"pending\"`, with no gateway call. The only payment code is `tests/test_payments.py`, which posts straight to a hardcoded sandbox URL. So the switch to the fake gateway is probably in a dependency, a deployment config, or a gateway client somewhere else. I noted that in the memory so nobody goes looking for it here.\n\nSo it can't trip anyone up silently again, I can do either of these:\n- **Make it loud:** if you tell me where the gateway gets chosen, I can add a structlog warning at startup whenever the fake gateway is active. Even better, I can make it fail in production-like environments unless the fake is explicitly requested.\n- **Document it:** add a short \"Environment variables\" section to the README listing `PAYMENTS_LIVE`, and also `EXPORT_BUCKET`, which `scripts/export.py` reads."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 783, "cache_read_input_tokens": 24514, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 783}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "dc270454-511f-4f9f-807b-03ea00ea2c58", "uuid": "402c70da-03eb-4990-80f1-13466f78eac8", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T13:06:03.063Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbZpP7pZXHCNPuhdDEhn"}
